Ohle Claussen wrote:

> On 2006-07-18, azgor wrote:
>> Rodney ideas[14]: Cursed amulets of lifesaving have a 50% chance of
>> not working, 49% chance of working, and 1% chance of working only
>> after you get your player information and see the tombstone.
> 
> The best thing about this is that when a player dies with an AoLS (or
> an unidentified amulet) on, they'd carefully copy all of the
> information about attributes and unidentified objects, fervently
> hoping that they'll hit the 2% chance of being able to use it. 
> 
> Of course, if they do, they have a massive advantage, but "you get a
> 1% chance of a massive advantage and a 50% chance of death with a
> special item" doesn't sound unbalancing to me.

The game could decide you have hit the 1% before displaying the inventory 
and then lie about the identity of just a few of the objects. That way the 
player thinks they've just identified everything but they haven't. Some 
tricky coding though to make sure the misidentified objects are plausibly 
misidentified.


